# Windows poster machine settings. Copy to .env and fill in.

# Where the reporter daemon ships events. Leave blank to run fully offline —
# events still queue in data/outbox.sqlite and flush once this is set.
REPORTER_URL=
REPORTER_TOKEN=

# Where `cl post` claims its next draft from. Without these the poster has
# nothing to post and will no-op — posting is fail-closed by design, it never
# invents an ad locally.
#
# QUEUE_URL is the /queue base on the same API as REPORTER_URL.
# MACHINE_TOKEN is issued in the dashboard under Settings -> Machine tokens and
# is shown exactly once. It is deliberately NOT the same value as
# REPORTER_TOKEN, so a compromised desktop can be revoked without breaking
# event ingest for everything else.
QUEUE_URL=
MACHINE_TOKEN=

# Optional overrides. Both default to this machine's hostname.
# CL_MACHINE=
# MACHINE_ID=

# Posts `cl edit-canary` is allowed to really edit, comma-separated. Anything
# not listed here is refused, so the canary can never be aimed at a live earning
# posting by a typo. Leave blank until you have a throwaway post to burn.
# CL_CANARY_POSTS=
